-- Road navigation (KNG-27): put back the 5 road profiles from the 2026-10-01 18:24 phpMyAdmin backup
-- (database knightsandkings_dev_v2, table road_profiles), after road-navigation-reset.sql deleted them.
--
-- Profiles restored (original ids 1-5 in the backup):
--   Default road, Cinix rural road, Cinix Keepstreet, Cinix Keepstreet Stair House, Stonebrick bridge
-- Materials, roles, ambiguous flags, widths, sample counts, Enabled, scope and learning stats exactly as in the backup.
--
-- Safe to run next to the profiles you made since:
--   - no Id is given: MySQL assigns new ids, so nothing collides with the new profiles' ids;
--   - a profile whose Name already exists is SKIPPED (names are unique) - the check at the end shows which.
-- Not restored: the old surveys/seeds/tiles/nodes/edges (they would point at the old ids and old network).
--
-- Mind: restored profiles are Enabled = 1 and take part in the next build. A material counts as ambiguous only when
-- EVERY enabled profile listing it flags it, so e.g. GRAVEL (unflagged in all five) becomes a sure road material again.
-- To bring them back switched off, run the UPDATE at the end of the script before COMMIT.
--
-- The JSON strings keep the backup's \" escaping (valid in MySQL's default sql_mode).

START TRANSACTION;

SELECT Id, Name, Enabled FROM road_profiles ORDER BY Id;   -- before

